    "q-108372": {
      "dom_id": "step-q108372",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Use a calculator to evaluate ${log}_{11}⁡(7)$ rounded to $3$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "Let's calculate ${log}_{11}⁡(7)$ by changing the base $11$ to the common logarithm (base $10$).\n\nWe use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}⁡X=\\frac{{log}_{b}⁡X}{{log}_{b}⁡a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=11,$ $X=7,$ $b=10.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{11}⁡(7) & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡(7)}{{log}_{10}⁡(11)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(11)} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{0.845\\,098}{1.041\\,393} \\\\  & ≈0.812\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
